3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,800
There's always room for additional competitors.

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,280
If you really want it to succeed, you just have to commit to it and spend time on it.

5
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:20,320
And so that's me with stuff, like it's something that I really care about.

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:23,840
I'm not just making a to do list app because that was the lowest hanging fruit.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,240
It's something that I really want to bring something to in that space.

8
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,320
I think that's why people love it.

9
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,440
Welcome to Launched.

10
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:32,560
I'm Charlie Chapman.

11
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:38,240
And today I'm excited to bring you the developer behind the aggressively delightful Tab task management app stuff.

12
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:39,680
Austin Blake.

13
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:54,960
Austin, welcome to the show.

14
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,320
Thank you very much.

15
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,080
I'm so glad to finally be here.

16
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,240
This is kind of like a dream because I've listened to your show for a long time, so it's kind of cool to be here.

17
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:05,760
Well, this is a timely episode actually for two different reasons.

18
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:23,040
So the first is, if I've done my math correct, this episode is going to come out on June 3, or at least right around there, which is right before WWDC, which is actually when I think that's when I first met you and you were telling me about this app that was I don't even know if it was in test flight yet, but it wasn't out called stuff.

19
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:23,600
Is that right?

20
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,200
That was like what two years ago?

21
